  "annotations": [
    {
      "id": "brand-note",
      "page": "page-1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "Brand values lifted from segsolar.com stylesheets: red #E00700, dark red #B51B16, blue #1C5CB0, Kanit headings, square corners (the site uses 0 radius outside circular elements).\nData shown is live data from the prototype's store: 2 suppliers, real item codes and quotes, backend-calculated scores 79 and 94."
    },
    {
      "id": "states-note",
      "page": "page-2",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 700,
      "text": "These three states are needed before the remaining backend rules land: blocking source roles until QC passes, and keeping voided records out of circulation.\nMessage text is copied from the API's own error strings."
    },
    {
      "id": "login-note",
      "page": "page-3",
      "x": 0,
      "y": -150,
      "w": 900,
      "text": "Three directions for the sign-in page, deliberately unlike the IT HelpDesk login (no image-left / form-right split, no rounded cards, no gray palette).\nB1 and B2 are the same layout solving the logo problem two ways: the white logo variant is built for dark backgrounds, so either the block goes dark (B1, mark untouched) or the mark is knocked out to pure white (B2, a derived asset marketing should approve)."
    }
  ],
